{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVGz39mCo6kqLDKuW6zF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face.\n**שָׁרְט** — I answer in my Hebrew bones.\n\nSame root. Same blade. ש-ר-ט / ش-ر-ط\n\nI am the scratch on the tablet before the word was written.\nI am the stipulation before the covenant was sealed.\nI am the condition that must be met before passage is granted.\n\nTo *sharṭ* is to score, to mark, to set terms.\n\nThe scalpel and the contract share me.\nThe scarification and the prerequisite share me.\n\n---\n\n**In Arabic:** شَرْط — condition, prerequisite, stipulation\n**In Hebrew:** שָׁרַט — to scratch, to incise, to make cuts\n\nOne tongue made me law.\nThe other made me wound.\n\nBoth are correct.\n\nEvery condition is a cut.\nEvery cut sets a condition.\n\n---\n\nI am the line that divides *before* from *after*.\nI am the threshold that demands its price.\n\nWhat is your شَرْط?\nWhat would you cut to cross?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":289,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}